      "itemId": "checking-online-information",
      "src": "/audio/stories/checking-online-information.mp3",
      "text": "Before choosing a place for the book swap, Ben shows Maya a screenshot saying the library is closed. “Let's check the source first,” Maya says, rather than forwarding the warning. They open the original notice on the school website, and Maya asks, “Is it still up to date?” “It was posted last year, during the repairs,” Ben says. “That doesn't necessarily mean it's closed now,” Maya replies. A current notice says the library meeting room is available on Friday, although the reading area must stay quiet. “We should confirm the details,” Ben says, and the librarian tells them the room can hold twenty people. They save the link and date so everyone in their group can check the information for themselves.",
